  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Reading Program Implementation and Expansion (NRPIE) Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Malawi):  USAID&apos;s National Reading Program Implementation and Expansion (NRPIE) activity provides technical assistance via a U.S. university partnership to the Ministry of Education&apos;s (MOE) Department of Quality Assurance and the Malawi Institute of Education. FY 2021 funds will be used to continue providing technical support from Florida State University (FSU) to the Malawi Institute of Education to: 1) develop upper primary level Chichewa and English teaching and learning materials, and 2) to align these materials to a revised Scope and Sequence. The activity will facilitate the transfer of technical skills from FSU to the Malawi Institute of Education to manage and sustain a comprehensive instructional material development system in line with its mandate to support the implementation of Malawi&apos;s national curriculum. .This activity supports the ICS Mission Objective 3.3 - Malawi expands educational opportunity to equip its citizens with foundational and marketable skills responsive to Malawi&apos;s public and private sector needs. The activity supports the Mission&apos;s strategy through endeavouring to strengthen capacities of a public sector institution through the transfer of skills and knowledge from U.S. higher education institutions to improve the quality of materials for use in service delivery..</narrative>
  </description>
